 national AI supercomputer\, leads two of the nine UKRI National AI Researc
 h Hubs (Collective Intelligence and Information Theory)\, runs UKRI Centre
 s for Doctoral Training in Interactive AI...\n\nOrganisation: University o
 f Bristol\, School of Computer Science\nLocation: Bristol\, England\, UK. 
 On campus\; part-time\, job-share and flexible working welcomed.\nAward: S
 alary GBP 43\,482 to 53\,253 per annum (Grade J) or GBP 50\,253 to 58\,225
  per annum (Grade K). Open-ended contract. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Open-ended (permanent) contract\, full-time\; part-time and job-share poss
 ible.\n\nMore: https://www.bristol.ac.uk/jobs/find/details/?jobId=391676&u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
